Description: Define _STAT_VER fallback for glibc 2.33+ compatibility
 glibc 2.33+ removed the _STAT_VER macro (the new stat ABI no longer uses
 versioned __xstat functions). fakeroot 1.20.2 still references _STAT_VER
 in libfakeroot.c, communicate.c, and libfakeroot_unix2003.c, causing
 build failures on Ubuntu 22.04 (glibc 2.35) and similar modern distros.
 .
 This patch adds a `#define _STAT_VER 1` fallback at the top of each
 affected source file. The value 1 matches _STAT_VER_LINUX on x86_64
 (the only platform supported by this buildroot's host-fakeroot).
 .
 The proper fix is to upgrade to fakeroot 1.25+ where the new stat ABI is
 handled, but this minimal patch keeps the existing recipe working.
Author: Sam <sam@etri.local>
Forwarded: not-needed (project-local fix for buildroot 2017.02 era)
Last-Update: 2026-05-14
--- a/libfakeroot.c
+++ b/libfakeroot.c
@@ -1,3 +1,7 @@
+#ifndef _STAT_VER
+#define _STAT_VER 1  /* glibc 2.33+ compat: was _STAT_VER_LINUX on x86_64 */
+#endif
